ldria. It has a transformer tender of about C$900M due to award in Q1 2027.\n- Norvane Utilities plans spending up 12%, with a C$450M tender in Q2 2027.\n- The plans are mostly for substations and transformers (n2.d2, n2.d7).\n- VLTX holdings won 60% of the last tender round. Its utility order intake has risen every quarter: C$610M in 2025Q4, 640 in Q1, 655 in Q2 and 670 in Q3 2026 (n2.d4).\n\n**Data centres (still growing, but slower)**\n- Grid connection requests are expected to grow 9% in 2027, slower than in 2026, because power availability limits new sites (n2.d3).\n- The connection queue grew 4% in Q3 2026. Data centres are 60% of new requests, and the average wait is 26 months (n2.d8). Long waits mean the demand is backed up rather than lost.\n\n**Risks and gaps**\n- Utility financing is a risk. Bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, and two utility share offerings were cut back in size (n5.d2, n6.d3). Financing constraints could delay or shrink the capex plans. Node n3 is assessing this.\n- I did not read the VLTX customer mix, so I can't say how much of VLTX's orders depend on each buyer.\n- The tender awards are plans, not signed orders.","ttft_ms":1470,"type":"result","duration_ms":38179,"uuid":"42179ae0-24a5-4ce3-ace8-2d6b6f3f1360","ttft_stream_ms":873,"time_to_request_ms":164,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":12,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":9,"input_attachments":48,"input_hooks":6,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":12,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":7,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":17},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":32,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":195,"process_anon_mib_turn_st